---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Why Choose Portland Sheep?" description="Why Portland sheep are well suited to smallholders, conservation grazing, showing, meat and wool production.">
  <div class="bg-sage-800 text-white py-20 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <p class="text-sage-300 text-sm uppercase tracking-widest mb-3">About</p>
      <h1 class="font-serif text-5xl mb-6">Why Choose Portland Sheep?</h1>
      <p class="text-cream-200 text-xl max-w-2xl">A historic, versatile breed with character, excellent wool and a natural place on today's smallholding.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-16">
    <nav class="flex gap-4 mb-12 border-b border-cream-200 pb-4 overflow-x-auto">
      {[['Overview', '/about/'], ['Why Portlands?', '/about/why-portland-sheep/'], ['History', '/about/history/'], ['Wool', '/about/wool/'], ['For the Table', '/about/for-the-table/']].map(([label, href]) => (
        <a href={href} class="text-sm font-medium text-gray-500 hover:text-sage-700 pb-4 -mb-4 border-b-2 border-transparent hover:border-sage-500 transition-colors whitespace-nowrap px-1">{label}</a>
      ))}
    </nav>

    <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none prose-headings:font-serif prose-headings:text-sage-800">
      <p>So why should you choose Portland Sheep for your flock, a breed steeped in history which is as popular today with smallholders?</p>
      <h2>A versatile breeding flock</h2>
      <p>Its almost unique ability to breed all year around has been passed to other Dorset breeds and is a useful trait to have within your flock should you choose.</p>
      <h2>Wool and meat</h2>
      <p>Its soft fleece is a delight to spin and is very sought after by hand-spinners and crafters.</p>
      <p>They convert low quality grasses into high quality meat, slowly developing into Hogget with a hint of a gamey flavour reminiscent of it past. <strong>Just remember you do need some vegetation, they do not live on mud!</strong></p>
      <h2>Smallholding and conservation grazing</h2>
      <p>Ideal for conservation grazing, and if you have a large lawn and hate your mower what better than a trio of Portlands? <em>They do need year round maintenance though and require more attention than your mower!</em></p>
      <p>Owing to their small size and ability to convert low quality grasses, Portlands are able to be kept at a higher density-per-acre than many other sheep.</p>
      <h2>Showing and character</h2>
      <p>In the show ring Portland sheep are calm, easy to handle and have a stand out personality, ideal for all who show be it a novice, young handler or experienced show person.</p>
      <p><strong>And above all, the gorgeous look, and a great personality , just the perfect little sheep.</strong> It may not behave for your dog, but have bucket of sheep nuts and you will have a friend. And who cannot appreciate the classic look of this handsome animal; when the Creator developed the stars and decided the lead sign of the Zodiac was Aries the Ram, who do you think they had in mind?</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
